  "deck_seconds": 84.3,
  "output_id": "o_b98e1633435e",
  "case": "The readers are funders whom board members will meet to talk about the sixth site. They must believe that need is outgrowing Harborlight's five sites and that a sixth site at the Eastgate branch library is a sound, proven way to meet it. The strongest evidence: enrollment rose from 936 to 1,148, and 287 adults were still on the waitlist at year end. Sixty-eight percent of learners who stayed at least 12 weeks gained a reading level, and the cost per learner was $1,237. Funders will ask whether the work works, who does it, what the site adds and what it costs. The ask is $190,000, the rise from the FY2026 operating expenses of $1,420,000 to the proposed FY2027 budget of $1,610,000, which adds the sixth site and two site coordinators.",
